  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shyghon vs The Food Safety Officer on 28 September, 2017 Author: Shaji P.Chaly Bench: Shaji P.Chaly In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice Shaji P.Chaly Monday, The 8Th Day Of January 2018 / 18Th Pousha, 1939 WP(C).No. 28318 of 2017 Petitioner: Shyghon,S/O.Jose,Aged 40 Years, Cheeran House,Pookode Village, Kottapady P.O.-680 505, Thrissur District (Managing Partner), M/S.Nine Star Associates, Jose Memorial Building, Kottappady P.O.-680 505,Thrissur District). By Advs.Sri.Santhosh Subramanian Sri.E.A.Thankappan Sri.Sherry J. Thomas Sri.S.Sreekumar(North Paravur) Respondent(S): 1. The Food Safety Officer, Guruvayoor Circle, Chavakkad P.O., Pin: 680 506,Thrissur District. 2. The Food Safety Officer, Thrissur Circle, M.G.Road, Thrissur-680 001. 3. Assistant Commissioner Of Food Safety, M.G.Road, Thrissur-680 001. 4. Commissioner Of Food Safety, Thykkadu, Thiruvananthapuram-695 001. 5. Sub Inspector Of Police, Shyghon vs The Food Safety Officer on 28 September, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/189751928/ 1 Vadakkekkadu Police Station, Punnayurkulam P.O.-679 561. *Addl.R6 Impleaded *Addl.R6: The Commissioner Of Commercial Taxes, State Of Kerala. *Addl.R6 Is Suo Motu Impleaded As Per Order Dated 28/9/2017. R1 To Addl . R6 By Spl.Government Pleader Sri.C.E.Unnikrishnan",
    "facts": "JUDGMENT Petitioners are registered owners of goods vehicle bearing Nos.KL.46.M 6587 and KL.7.Q 919. In the vehicles parked by the side of the road, goods prohibited for sale under the Food Safety and Standards Act (herein after referred to as `FSS Act' for short) was found out and the vehicles consequently were taken possession of by the foods safety authority and removed to the concerned Police Stations. 2. The legal contention advanced is that even though the Foods Safety authority is entitled to take samples of the products found in the vehicle, they are not vested with the powers under the FSS Act or any other Rules to detain the vehicle. It is thus seeking appropriate directions, this writ petition is filed. 3 concerned Commissioner of Commercial Tax is suo motu impleaded to this writ petition.",
